.TH BB\-CLI 1 "September 2026" "bb-cli 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bb\-cli \- Bitbucket from the command line
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bb\-cli
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bb\-cli
is to Bitbucket Cloud what
.BR gh (1)
is to GitHub: pull requests, pipelines, branches and build statuses from a
terminal, without opening a browser and without hand\-rolling
.BR curl (1)
calls.
.PP
It is a single bash script. It needs
.BR curl ,
.BR jq
and
.BR git ,
and authenticates over HTTP Basic with an Atlassian API token.
.PP
Anything the named commands do not cover is reachable through
.BR "bb\-cli api" ,
an authenticated passthrough to the REST API. Reaching for
.BR curl
directly should be treated as a missing feature.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Reading
.TP
.B pr \fR[\fInumber\fR] [\fIoptions\fR]
List pull requests, or show one in detail including its description. Filters:
.BR \-\-branch ,
.BR \-\-target ,
.BR \-\-author ,
.BR \-\-state ,
.BR \-\-limit .
.B \-j
returns raw JSON,
.B \-c
includes comments. Subcommands mirror
.BR gh (1):
.BR "view <n>" ,
.BR "checks <n>" ,
.BR "edit <n>" ,
.BR "ready <n>" ,
.BR "comment <n>" .
.TP
.B pr edit \fIn\fR [\fB\-\-title\fI t\fR] [\fB\-\-body\-file\fI f\fR]
Change a pull request's title, description, or both. The current values are read
first and both fields are sent, so changing one cannot blank the other. Use
.B \-\-body\-file
rather than an inline string: markdown hard breaks are trailing spaces, and
command substitution strips them.
.TP
.B pr checks \fIn\fR
The build statuses on the pull request's head commit \- including any published
by
.BR "bb\-cli signoff" .
.TP
.B pipeline \fR[\fInumber\fR] [\fIsubcommand\fR]
List pipelines, or show one with its steps. Subcommands:
.BR steps ,
.BR "step <uuid> \-\-log" ,
.BR failures ,
.BR "trigger \-\-branch <b> [\-\-custom <name>]" ,
.BR "rerun <n>" ,
.BR "cancel <n>" ,
.BR "watch <n> [\-\-exit\-status]" .
Flags may appear before or after the subcommand.
.BR run
is accepted as a synonym, since that is
.BR gh 's
noun for the same object.
.TP
.B branch \fR[\fIfilter\fR]
List branches, most recently updated first.
.TP
.B cache \fR[\fBlist\fR|\fBdelete\fI uuid\fR]
Pipeline caches, the counterpart of
.BR "gh cache" .
Deletion is by uuid only: Bitbucket also accepts a name, and that removes every
cache sharing it, on every branch.
.TP
.B repo
Repository metadata: description, default branch, size, language.
.SS Writing
.TP
.B signoff \fR[\fIoptions\fR]
Publish a build status on a commit from the result of a local run, the
counterpart of
.BR "gh signoff" .
Defaults to
.B SUCCESSFUL
on
.BR HEAD ,
with key
.BR local\-signoff .
Refuses on a dirty working tree or an unpushed commit unless
.B \-\-force
is given. Needs only
.BR read:repository:bitbucket .
.TP
.B signoff status \fR[\fB\-\-commit\fI rev\fR]
List every build status on a commit, including ones published by pipelines and
third\-party integrations.
.SS Escape hatch
.TP
.B api \fIendpoint\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
Authenticated passthrough to the Bitbucket REST API. Paths are resolved under
.I https://api.bitbucket.org/2.0/
unless they already begin with
.I 2.0/
or
.IR internal/ .
The placeholders
.BR :repo ,
.B :workspace
and
.B :slug
expand from the git remote.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-X " method"
HTTP method. Default GET, or POST when \fB\-\-input\fR is given. Unlike
.BR "gh api" ,
fields alone do not imply POST: on Bitbucket a POST to
.I /pullrequests
creates a pull request.
.TP
.BI \-f " key=value"
String field. A query parameter on GET, a JSON field on a write.
.TP
.BI \-F " key=value"
Typed field: booleans, null and numbers stay unquoted;
.BI @ file
reads the value from a file.
.TP
.BI \-\-input " file"
Request body, verbatim.
.B \-
reads stdin. Use this for anything multi\-line: it preserves trailing
whitespace, which shell quoting does not.
.TP
.BI \-q " expression"
Filter the response through jq.
.TP
.B \-i
Print response headers.
.B x\-oauth\-scopes
there is the definitive answer to what a token can do.
.TP
.B \-\-paginate
Follow
.I next
links and merge every page's
.I .values
into one array.
.RE
.SS Setup and discovery
.TP
.B login \fR[\fB--with-token\fR] [\fB--email\fI email\fR]
Store an Atlassian API token. Interactive by default: it prints which scopes to
check, then prompts. With
.B --with-token
it reads the token from standard input and prompts for nothing, which is the
form a script, a CI job or an agent can complete; the account email then comes
from
.BR --email ,
else
.BR $BITBUCKET_USERNAME ,
else
.BR "git config user.email" .
The credential is verified against the API before anything is written. A bare
.B login
with no terminal exits 1 rather than consuming an invisible prompt.
.TP
.B logout
Remove stored credentials.
.TP
.B status
Show authentication status and the resolved repository.
.TP
.B docs \fR[\fItopic\fR]
Print the bundled documentation. Topics:
.BR setup ,
.BR scopes ,
.BR api ,
.BR pipelines ,
.BR signoff .
.TP
.B man
Open this page.
.TP
.B skill install \fR[\fB\-\-dir\fI dir\fR] [\fB\-\-project\fR]
Install the bundled Claude Code skill, so an AI agent on a machine that has
never seen bb\-cli knows what it is and how to drive it.
.TP
.B version
Print the version.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-R ", " \-\-repo " workspace/slug"
Act on a repository other than the one the current directory belongs to.
Accepts
.I workspace/slug
or a full Bitbucket URL. Required when running outside a checkout.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Every command accepts this.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/bb\-cli/credentials
Shell file, sourced at startup. Mode 600 in a 700 directory.
.RS
.PP
.nf
BITBUCKET_USERNAME=<atlassian email>
BITBUCKET_API_TOKEN=<token>
.fi
.RE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B BITBUCKET_USERNAME
.TQ
.B BITBUCKET_API_TOKEN
Take precedence over the credentials file, which is then never read. Useful in
CI and for trying a token without editing the file.
.TP
.B BITBUCKET_APP_PASSWORD
Accepted as a legacy alias for
.BR BITBUCKET_API_TOKEN .
.SH TOKEN SCOPES
Create the token at
.I id.atlassian.com
under Security, API tokens, "Create API token with scopes", choosing the
Bitbucket app. Check exactly five:
.PP
.nf
read:repository:bitbucket     write:pipeline:bitbucket
read:pullrequest:bitbucket    write:pullrequest:bitbucket
read:pipeline:bitbucket
.fi
.PP
Two traps:
.B write
does not imply
.BR read ,
so both halves of each pair must be checked; and scopes are fixed at creation,
so a token cannot gain one later.
.PP
.B admin:repository:bitbucket
is deliberately not in that list. It is what branch restrictions require, to
read as well as to write, and that policy is not a developer credential's to
edit.
.PP
Run
.B bb\-cli docs scopes
for what each command needs, which scopes look necessary and are not, and how
to prove what a token holds from the response headers.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
An error, including any HTTP status of 400 or above. The response body is still
printed, because Bitbucket's error bodies name the missing scope or field.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Sign off on a local test run:
.PP
.nf
.RS
npm test && bb\-cli signoff \-\-name "vitest 461 passed, 8s"
.RE
.fi
.PP
Read a pull request's description without leaving the terminal:
.PP
.nf
.RS
bb\-cli api repositories/:repo/pullrequests/10 \-q .description
.RE
.fi
.PP
Rewrite a pull request body from a file, byte for byte:
.PP
.nf
.RS
bb\-cli api repositories/:repo/pullrequests/10 \-X PUT \-\-input body.json
.RE
.fi
.PP
Find out what the current token is actually allowed to do:
.PP
.nf
.RS
bb\-cli api repositories/:repo \-i | grep \-i oauth
.RE
.fi
.PP
Trigger a custom pipeline on a branch and wait for it:
.PP
.nf
.RS
bb\-cli pipeline trigger \-\-branch my\-branch \-\-custom "Unit specs"
bb\-cli pipeline watch 1241 \-\-exit\-status
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gh (1),
.BR jq (1),
.BR git (1)
.PP
.B bb\-cli docs
for the full documentation set, which ships in the repository.
.SH BUGS
Bitbucket's public REST API has no endpoint for rerunning only the failed steps
of a pipeline, although the web UI offers it.
.B bb\-cli pipeline rerun \-\-failed
says so rather than quietly doing something else.
